Step 1: Create ASP.NET Core MVC Project
      1. Open Visual Studio 2026.
      2. Click Create a new project.
      3. Select ASP.NET Core Web App (Model-View-Controller).
      4. Project Name: SWOfflinePWA
      5. Framework: .NET 10 or the latest available.
Click Create.
Step 2: Create Home Page
In Solution Explorer, open:
Views > Home > Index.cshtml
Replace the code with:
<div class="text-center">
     <h1>College Information Portal</h1>
     <h3>PWA Offline Demo</h3>
     <p>This application works without internet connection.</p>
</div>
Step 3: Create Manifest File
      1. Right-click wwwroot.
      2. Select Add > New Item.
      3. Choose JSON File.
      4. Name it manifest.json.
Write the following:
{
    "name": "Offline PWA",
    "short_name": "OfflinePWA",
    "start_url": "/",
    "display": "standalone",
    "background_color": "#ffffff",
    "theme_color": "#0d6efd",
    "icons": [
        {
            "src": "/icons/icon1.png",
            "sizes": "192x192",
            "type": "image/png"
        },
        {
            "src": "/icons/icon2.png",
            "sizes": "512x512",
            "type": "image/png"
        }
    ]
}
Step 4: Create Icons Folder
            1. Right-click wwwroot.
            2. Select Add > New Folder.
            3. Name it icons.
            4. Add two downloaded icon files inside the folder:
                   o   icon1.png
                  o   icon2.png
Step 5: Create Service Worker
Inside wwwroot:
      1. Select Add > New Item.
      2. Choose JavaScript File.
      3. Name it service-worker.js.
Write the following code:
const CACHE_NAME = "pwa-cache-v1";
const urlsToCache = [
     "/Home/Index"
];
self.addEventListener("install", event => {
     event.waitUntil(
          caches.open(CACHE_NAME)
            .then(cache => {
                 return cache.addAll(urlsToCache);
            })
     );
});
self.addEventListener("fetch", event => {
     event.respondWith(
          caches.match(event.request)
            .then(response => {
                 return response || fetch(event.request);
            })
     );
});
Step 6: Register Manifest
In Solution Explorer, open:
Views > Shared > _Layout.cshtml
Inside the <head> tag, add:
<link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.json">
Step 7: Register Service Worker
Before the closing </body> tag, add:
<script>
     if ('serviceWorker' in navigator) {
          navigator.serviceWorker.register('/service-worker.js')
            .then(() => console.log('Service Worker Registered'));
     }
</script>
Step 8: Verify Static Files
In Solution Explorer, open Program.cs.
Ensure the following code exists. If it does not, add it before mapping the routes:
app.UseStaticFiles();
Step 9: Run Application
Run the ASP.NET Core MVC application from Visual Studio.
Step 10: Verify Service Worker
Open Developer Tools in the browser:
     1. Press F12.
     2. Open Application.
     3. Select Service Workers.
     4. Ensure service-worker.js is activated and running.
Step 11: Test Offline Mode
     1. Open Developer Tools by pressing F12.
     2. Select the Network tab.
     3. Select Offline.
     4. Refresh the webpage.
